      "message": "Sorry if my comment was misleading. The existing tests (before this CL) should cover already cover that.\n\n\u003e How does the empty suffix case being tested here differ from the unset suffix case and why?\n\nReplying to radical@ \u0027s comment, the suffix attribute is already defaulted to `\"\"`. Ideally, `suffix: \"\"` or unset `suffix` in Android.bp should result to the same BUILD which is that `suffix` is unset and defaulted to `\"\"`.\n\nIt\u0027s up to you if you want to pass in `suffix \u003d \"\"` in BUILD though.",
