      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T19:39:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry if this comment was also misleading.\n\nIn aosp/1999871, we add `suffix` attribute to `cc_library_shared` and `cc_binary`.\n\nAccording to the tests in this CL, we convert\n\n```\ncc_library_shared {\n  name: \"foo_shared\",\n  suffix: \"-suf\",\n}\n```\nto \n```\ncc_library_shared(\n  name  \u003d \"foo_shared-suf\"\n)\n```\nin bp2build/cc_library_shared_conversion_test.go\n\nand\n\n```\ncc_binary{\n  name: \"foo\",\n  suffix: \"\",\n}\n```\n\nto\n\n```\ncc_binary(\n  name \u003d \"foo\",\n  suffix \u003d \"\",\n)\n```\nin bp2build/cc_binary_conversion_test.go.\n\nIt doesn\u0027t quite make sense to me why we need the suffix attribute in Bazel and always pass empty string \"\" to it. Moreover, aosp/199987 has `suffix` defaulted to `\"\"` in the macros already.\n\nThe conflicting part is why `suffix` is handled inconsistently like this.\n1. When suffix is non-empty string, we append it to `name` attribute in Bazel.\n2. When suffix is empty string, we pass empty string to suffix attribute in Bazel.\n\nIt seems to me that we don\u0027t need to add another attribute (e.g. suffix) to convert suffix prop. Another solution is creating `soname` with the suffix value (and name if `soname` is empty) and moving resulted `soname` to BUILD instead.\n\nIn the test examples above,the resulted BUILD can be either\n\n```\ncc_library_shared(\n  name  \u003d \"foo_shared-suf\"\n)\ncc_binary(\n  name \u003d \"foo\",\n)\n```\n\nor \n\n```\ncc_library_shared(\n  name  \u003d \"foo_shared\",\n  suffix \u003d \"-suf\"\n)\ncc_binary(\n  name \u003d \"foo\",\n  suffix \u003d \"\"\n)\n```\n\nor even\n\n```\ncc_library_shared(\n  name  \u003d \"foo_shared\",\n  suffix \u003d \"-suf\"\n)\ncc_binary(\n  name \u003d \"foo\",\n  // because suffix is defaulted to \"\", don\u0027t need to set it.\n)\n```\n\nThe bottom line is we should handle/convert suffix prop consistently.\n\nThoughts?",
